1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP05 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:09,460
(Behind-the-Scenes)

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,750
Come on, teach me.

5
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:12,510
I'll teach you something simple.

6
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:12,900
Okay.

7
00:00:14,830 --> 00:00:15,270
Wait.

8
00:00:15,270 --> 00:00:16,390
You need to tell me a song

9
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:17,310
before I can teach you how to play it.

10
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:18,310
Any song you know.

11
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:19,310
Colorful Clouds Chasing the Moon?

12
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:22,430
Which part do you want to start with?

13
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:25,220
Okay.

14
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:28,940
(Demonstrating step by step)

15
00:00:29,670 --> 00:00:30,230
Or...

16
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:30,940
(Focused)

17
00:00:33,630 --> 00:00:34,630
For example.

18
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:37,910
It does slip around a bit.

19
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:39,190
Like this.

20
00:00:39,190 --> 00:00:40,190
This part is a little tricky.

21
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:45,110
Is it these two fingers or these two?

22
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,140
Three, four.

23
00:00:49,070 --> 00:00:49,860
Teach me how to sing.

24
00:00:52,140 --> 00:00:52,710
You teach me how to sing.

25
00:00:52,710 --> 00:00:53,510
Your teacher's right here.

26
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,180
Sing?

27
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:56,910
You're a vocal teacher.

28
00:00:56,910 --> 00:00:57,910
I'm not.

29
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:03,260
"Genius".

30
00:01:03,260 --> 00:01:04,390
That's what you call a "genius".

31
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:05,360
I'm already "off-key".

32
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:06,240
You pick it up just by watching.

33
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,070
"Help!"

34
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:08,340
That's great composition.

35
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:08,980
Great composition.

36
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:10,700
Yeah, great composition.

37
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:11,540
Sorry.

38
00:01:11,660 --> 00:01:16,620
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

39
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:17,540
(Behind-the-Scenes)

40
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:18,230
Oh my gosh.

41
00:01:18,670 --> 00:01:19,150
Wow.

42
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:19,470
Seriously.

43
00:01:19,470 --> 00:01:20,470
I went

44
00:01:20,470 --> 00:01:23,140
on a goodbye date today.

45
00:01:24,070 --> 00:01:24,950
Yeah.

46
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:28,350
But honestly, I feel like

47
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:30,070
if this were your "movie",

48
00:01:30,430 --> 00:01:31,510
this would be, like,

49
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:35,070
the first 30% of it.

50
00:01:35,190 --> 00:01:36,830
It's just the first part of your story.

51
00:01:36,830 --> 00:01:38,430
Once that little story ends,

52
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:39,390
that's when you start

53
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:42,780
to "transform".

54
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:43,980
And then, you know.

55
00:01:44,350 --> 00:01:46,620
You become a better version of yourself

56
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:48,460
after a major change.

57
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:50,390
Yeah, and you become braver.

58
00:01:51,190 --> 00:01:53,030
Now you can start following

59
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:54,710
the "main storyline".

60
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:56,110
Tell me how I'm supposed to do that.

61
00:01:56,390 --> 00:01:58,030
Just do it normally.

62
00:01:58,310 --> 00:02:00,260
Just be yourself.

63
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:01,820
Okay. We'll just be ourselves.

64
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:02,830
Yeah.

65
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:09,900
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

66
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:10,820
(Behind-the-Scenes)

67
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:12,630
My shrink plastic sheets
finally arrived.

68
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:14,790
You bought so many.

69
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:15,900
There are only ten sheets.

70
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:18,820
(First attempt
at making shrink plastic failed)

71
00:02:20,230 --> 00:02:21,830
Is it a problem with the paper?

72
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:23,780
(Realizing)

73
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:28,270
As expected, it's different.

74
00:02:29,510 --> 00:02:30,310
Really?

75
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:31,780
(Feeling it)

76
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:34,190
I can really feel the difference.

77
00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:35,230
Yeah.

78
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:38,590
You just saved the whole world.

79
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:44,830
How small can it shrink?

80
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:46,670
Can it shrink down to this size?

81
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:47,550
About that much.

82
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,310
It's okay. You can decide.

83
00:02:50,310 --> 00:02:51,430
They both look good.

84
00:02:53,350 --> 00:02:54,340
If you mess up...

85
00:02:55,830 --> 00:02:57,060
we still have more.

86
00:02:57,060 --> 00:02:58,220
There are plenty.

87
00:02:58,540 --> 00:02:59,580
We've got plenty of backups.

88
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:00,220
Yeah.

89
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:03,740
(Starting to draw)

90
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:07,580
(Glances)

91
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,820
(Leaning closer)

92
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:18,460
(Giggling)

93
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:22,350
It feels so much more vibrant
than last time.

94
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:24,190
The paper you bought is better.

95
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,260
Why are you laughing?

96
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:37,110
I'm amazed you're so good with words.

97
00:03:37,670 --> 00:03:39,990
You taught me.

98
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:42,260
Little by little.

99
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:47,230
You must be a really fast learner.

100
00:03:48,470 --> 00:03:49,710
I take learning seriously.

101
00:03:55,700 --> 00:04:00,660
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

102
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:02,360
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I loved watching

103
00:04:02,360 --> 00:04:03,510
The Racing Brothers Let's & Go!!
as a kid.

104
00:04:05,270 --> 00:04:06,740
I watched it too.

105
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:07,540
I even bought some of the toys.

106
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:08,990
Did you watch Balala the Fairies?

107
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:11,790
Not really. The thing is,

108
00:04:12,150 --> 00:04:14,630
they had to go through

109
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:16,950
this long transformation
before every fight.

110
00:04:17,230 --> 00:04:18,390
"Gunala, God of Darkness!"

111
00:04:19,110 --> 00:04:20,020
(Laughs)
I don't get it.

112
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:20,820
"Woohoo Lahoo!"

113
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,580
"Dark Magic Transformation!"

114
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,790
I can't stand
these drawn-out transformations.

115
00:04:25,790 --> 00:04:26,750
Did you ever think about

116
00:04:26,750 --> 00:04:27,910
how Ultraman always waited

117
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:30,820
until the last second
to use their ultimate move?

118
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:31,700
Why couldn't they just use it

119
00:04:31,700 --> 00:04:32,580
right away and finish the fight?

120
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:33,630
Why did they have to wait

121
00:04:34,030 --> 00:04:35,070
until their light turned red,

122
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:36,030
then suddenly remember

123
00:04:36,030 --> 00:04:36,670
they had this ultimate move?

124
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:37,830
Yeah, that light was always going
to turn red.

125
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:41,070
It's kind of like Pokemon.

126
00:04:41,150 --> 00:04:41,580
Yeah.

127
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,950
Someone has to be near death

128
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:46,790
before you can unleash new power.

129
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:48,630
Maybe that's exactly why

130
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:50,310
we loved these shows so much as kids.

131
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:52,630
It's just that now that we're grown up,

132
00:04:52,630 --> 00:04:53,830
we look at that part

133
00:04:54,260 --> 00:04:54,860
and think it's ridiculous,

134
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:56,150
but also kind of hilarious.

135
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:57,660
Maybe I'm just childish,

136
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:58,660
but sometimes

137
00:04:58,660 --> 00:04:59,950
I still get into that feeling.

138
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:01,190
Like, say your

139
00:05:01,550 --> 00:05:03,020
when your teammate gets hurt,

140
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:04,350
and then suddenly...

141
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:05,700
You start spinning around to transform.

142
00:05:06,150 --> 00:05:08,190
I wouldn't spin around
and transform before a fight.

143
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:11,350
Which Ultraman is your favorite?

144
00:05:11,350 --> 00:05:11,980
(Asks)

145
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:13,590
I got into Ultraman with Tiga.

146
00:05:13,590 --> 00:05:14,260
Tiga. Got it.

147
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:15,140
Back then, I was so...

148
00:05:15,140 --> 00:05:15,940
Even now that I think about it,

149
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:16,500
I still feel like

150
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:17,750
it'd be hilarious if I told you.

151
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:18,270
You know?

152
00:05:18,870 --> 00:05:20,660
Back then, I told my grandma

153
00:05:20,660 --> 00:05:22,150
the two of us

154
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:23,550
should go out the next day.

155
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:24,390
She asked why.

156
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:25,710
I said I wanted to look
for the Sparklens.

157
00:05:26,270 --> 00:05:27,700
Then she asked

158
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:28,260
where we were going.

159
00:05:28,260 --> 00:05:29,140
I said we had to go to Yunnan.

160
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:29,820
She asked why.

161
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:31,820
I said the Sparklens was hidden deep
in the mountains.

162
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:33,510
It didn't just appear anywhere.

163
00:05:33,510 --> 00:05:34,340
We have to go deep

164
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:35,310
into the mountains to find it.

165
00:05:40,060 --> 00:05:45,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

166
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,350
(Behind-the-Scenes)

167
00:05:46,350 --> 00:05:49,510
Describe the first impression
in one word.

168
00:05:50,590 --> 00:05:51,950
One word? First impression?

169
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:53,340
(First Impression)

170
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:55,060
(Thinking)

171
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:56,030
How about this?

172
00:05:56,030 --> 00:05:57,190
Two words.

173
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:58,230
One for the first impression,

174
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:00,150
(First & Current Impression)
and one for the current impression.

175
00:06:01,950 --> 00:06:02,670
Sure.

176
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:03,990
A word that sums it all up.

177
00:06:10,110 --> 00:06:10,870
Okay, I'm done.

178
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:11,550
I'm ready.

179
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,740
(Glances)

180
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:15,830
Is there anything you're curious about?

181
00:06:16,220 --> 00:06:17,980
(First Impression: Shy.
Current Impression: Simple)

182
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:19,540
(Glances)

183
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:22,110
It doesn't seem that difficult.

184
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:24,150
Can you see this?

185
00:06:26,780 --> 00:06:28,380
(Moving closer)

186
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:29,990
Sensitive.

187
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:31,150
(First Impression: Sensitive)

188
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:31,950
Steady.

189
00:06:32,230 --> 00:06:33,990
(Current Impression: Steady)
Actually, when I first met you,

190
00:06:33,990 --> 00:06:34,430
I thought

191
00:06:34,430 --> 00:06:36,150
you were a sensitive person.

192
00:06:36,990 --> 00:06:37,790
Why?

193
00:06:39,910 --> 00:06:42,070
It was your eyes.

194
00:06:42,390 --> 00:06:43,910
And all those little details.

195
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:45,230
You were observing everyone.

196
00:06:46,390 --> 00:06:47,670
You noticed that?

197
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:49,340
(Grabbing)

198
00:06:51,110 --> 00:06:53,270
You're pretty observant too.

199
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:57,110
And now, I think

200
00:06:57,110 --> 00:06:57,990
you're steady.

201
00:06:57,990 --> 00:06:58,950
Stable, basically.

202
00:06:58,950 --> 00:07:00,430
You're calm and even-keeled.

203
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:02,670
You don't have many emotional
ups and downs.

204
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:04,390
That's how I see you now.

205
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:10,950
Actually, I'm still pretty curious.

206
00:07:11,550 --> 00:07:12,470
Yesterday, on Chill Day, you said

207
00:07:12,470 --> 00:07:13,270
you'd already thought about

208
00:07:13,270 --> 00:07:15,190
what you'd say if I came up.

209
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:17,820
(Curious)

210
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,390
Honestly, I was thinking of saying...

211
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,190
You mentioned before

212
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:22,990
that you're pretty rational at work,

213
00:07:22,990 --> 00:07:24,430
but maybe not as much in everyday life.

214
00:07:24,860 --> 00:07:28,060
I actually hope that at work,

215
00:07:28,550 --> 00:07:30,270
you can think
about yourself a little more.

216
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:33,620
(Nods)

217
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:34,700
That's it?

218
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:47,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

219
00:07:48,310 --> 00:07:49,670
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Why are you taking pictures again?

220
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:50,860
(Hold it in place)

221
00:07:51,190 --> 00:07:51,990
Come in.

222
00:07:53,100 --> 00:07:54,540
Hi, everyone.

223
00:07:55,550 --> 00:07:55,990
Hello.

224
00:07:55,990 --> 00:07:56,710
Do you want a picture?

225
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:57,790
Come on, together.

226
00:07:57,870 --> 00:07:59,620
Get ready. Let's take a picture.

227
00:07:59,780 --> 00:08:00,580
Come on.

228
00:08:01,430 --> 00:08:03,590
This should gradually fade out,

229
00:08:03,590 --> 00:08:05,190
and then it'll flash once it's gone.

230
00:08:05,190 --> 00:08:06,670
Okay, everyone?

231
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:07,990
Okay.

232
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:09,270
Over here?

233
00:08:09,270 --> 00:08:09,970
Come on, we're ready.

234
00:08:09,970 --> 00:08:10,770
Do you want to take off the blanket?

235
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:11,990
I'm not taking it off.

236
00:08:12,310 --> 00:08:13,470
This is my outfit for today.

237
00:08:13,470 --> 00:08:14,190
(Today's outfit)

238
00:08:14,190 --> 00:08:14,870
Okay.

239
00:08:16,390 --> 00:08:18,620
Okay, did you two in the back hear me?

240
00:08:19,710 --> 00:08:20,580
Did you hear that?

241
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:21,230
Yes.

242
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:23,780
You two.

243
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:25,270
We can't have you two spread out.

244
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:27,010
You stay in the middle. That's fine.

245
00:08:27,010 --> 00:08:27,540
Right in the middle.

246
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:28,110
Okay, that's good.

247
00:08:28,470 --> 00:08:29,910
Okay, Fang, you need to show yourself.

248
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:31,100
Okay.

249
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:32,380
Hurry.

250
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,180
Come on.

251
00:08:39,270 --> 00:08:40,550
We all look so good.

252
00:08:41,590 --> 00:08:42,420
I'll go get some bread.

253
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:42,820
Okay.

254
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:44,180
(Glances)

255
00:08:44,710 --> 00:08:46,070
I'll take a picture of you two.

256
00:08:46,070 --> 00:08:47,390
Yu Yang, Fang.

257
00:08:47,830 --> 00:08:49,910
Thanks. Should we pose like this?

258
00:08:50,550 --> 00:08:53,270
We... My outfit today is really...

259
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:55,430
(Getting closer)
Pink and cute.

260
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:57,580
(Move over)

261
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:00,100
Three,

262
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:01,140
two,

263
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:01,820
one.

264
00:09:03,990 --> 00:09:05,150
This looks amazing.

265
00:09:05,150 --> 00:09:05,780
Thank you.

266
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:06,710
Thanks.

267
00:09:07,060 --> 00:09:12,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

268
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:12,740
(Behind-the-Scenes)

269
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:13,660
(Notices)

270
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:16,110
What's wrong with you?

271
00:09:16,230 --> 00:09:17,310
I feel like I'm coming down with a cold.

272
00:09:17,310 --> 00:09:19,110
Maybe it's because the weather
is a little cold today.

273
00:09:19,550 --> 00:09:20,950
It's definitely cold today.

274
00:09:21,190 --> 00:09:21,870
Come on, let's go back.

275
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:22,500
Let's go.

276
00:09:23,030 --> 00:09:24,190
We'll head upstairs first.

277
00:09:24,710 --> 00:09:25,380
Bye bye.

278
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:26,030
Bye.

279
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,900
(Stops)

280
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:32,740
(Comes closer)

281
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,270
Can you tell what I was trying to say?

282
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:37,790
What?

283
00:09:38,230 --> 00:09:38,790
Good night.

284
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:39,870
(Good night)

285
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:40,500
You guessed it.

286
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:41,100
Did I?

287
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:41,900
Yeah.

288
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:44,020
Then let's...

289
00:09:44,660 --> 00:09:45,340
Sit for a bit.

290
00:09:47,150 --> 00:09:48,270
You can take some medicine.

291
00:09:48,270 --> 00:09:49,500
(Worried)

292
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:51,470
I think I'll be fine
if I drink some hot water.

293
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:52,700
Still, you should take something

294
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:53,540
just in case.

295
00:09:54,030 --> 00:09:55,470
Do you want some? I have cold medicine.

296
00:09:55,710 --> 00:09:57,070
No, I'm fine. I don't get sick.

297
00:09:57,070 --> 00:09:58,550
I rarely get sick.

298
00:09:58,710 --> 00:10:00,950
Don't say that.

299
00:10:01,590 --> 00:10:03,670
I haven't been to the hospital
in over a year.

300
00:10:03,670 --> 00:10:04,660
I haven't taken any medicine either.

301
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:05,430
That's great.

302
00:10:05,430 --> 00:10:06,630
I hope you never need to see a doctor

303
00:10:06,630 --> 00:10:07,310
or take medicine.

304
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:13,070
This is my first time
wearing dark-colored clothes.

305
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:15,980
(Observing closely)

306
00:10:17,110 --> 00:10:19,230
Then I have to make sure
I remember this.

307
00:10:20,030 --> 00:10:22,670
I'll record it with my eyes.

308
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:30,780
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

309
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:32,260
(Behind-the-Scenes)

310
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:33,510
My handwriting is really ugly.

311
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:34,750
I didn't practice

312
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:35,630
(Thinking)
as a kid.

313
00:10:36,230 --> 00:10:37,150
It could use some work.

314
00:10:37,390 --> 00:10:38,350
That's true.

315
00:10:39,110 --> 00:10:40,070
That's a very tactful way to put it.

316
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:41,070
(Amused)

317
00:10:41,070 --> 00:10:42,630
There's a lot of room for improvement.

318
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,790
I even studied calligraphy for a while.

319
00:10:45,790 --> 00:10:47,150
But I really couldn't sit still.

320
00:10:48,430 --> 00:10:50,430
My first class was just drawing circles
over and over.

321
00:10:50,890 --> 00:10:51,890
Drawing circles
with a calligraphy brush.

322
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:53,190
Can you draw a perfect circle?

323
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:55,590
It doesn't matter
if your circle is perfect.

324
00:10:55,590 --> 00:10:56,550
You just have to keep drawing.

325
00:10:56,550 --> 00:10:58,430
You have to calm your mind.

326
00:10:58,430 --> 00:11:00,870
But I feel like
you're actually pretty patient.

327
00:11:07,550 --> 00:11:11,030
(Whispering)
When is our macaroni coming?

328
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:15,220
So embarrassing.

329
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:17,230
I'm still hungry.

330
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:19,460
It's okay.

331
00:11:19,990 --> 00:11:20,790
I ordered it.

332
00:11:20,790 --> 00:11:21,820
And you happened to want some,

333
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:23,380
so I'll share a little with you.

334
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:24,220
Yeah.

335
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:26,150
You ordered it.

336
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:34,500
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

337
00:11:34,540 --> 00:11:35,860
(Behind-the-Scenes)

338
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:36,830
This photo looks good.

339
00:11:38,150 --> 00:11:39,430
It's also one of my favorites.

340
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:42,310
It's really good.

341
00:11:43,950 --> 00:11:44,790
Xing.

342
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:45,750
I feel like this one

343
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:46,670
looks good too.

344
00:11:49,630 --> 00:11:50,750
I like this one.

345
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:55,980
It really brings out your beauty.

346
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:57,060
(Laughs)

347
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:57,540
Okay.

348
00:12:10,150 --> 00:12:11,310
(Caring)
Are you tired?

349
00:12:11,630 --> 00:12:13,270
No, my eyes just feel a little dry.

350
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:14,670
Then I'll head inside.

351
00:12:14,670 --> 00:12:15,350
Okay.

352
00:12:15,350 --> 00:12:16,550
Go back and get some rest.

353
00:12:16,550 --> 00:12:19,250
Xing, don't you have any eye drops?

354
00:12:19,250 --> 00:12:19,870
It's okay.

355
00:12:19,870 --> 00:12:21,190
(Concerned)
I'll take out my contact lenses later.

356
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:22,950
Okay, Xing.

357
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:23,950
Go back and get some rest.

358
00:12:23,950 --> 00:12:24,660
Okay, then.

359
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:25,060
Bye bye.

360
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:25,630
Okay. Get some rest.

361
00:12:26,070 --> 00:12:26,620
Bye bye.

362
00:12:26,620 --> 00:12:27,230
Bye.

363
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:33,940
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

364
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:36,340
(Behind-the-Scenes)

365
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:37,910
(Offering)
How about I take a picture of you guys?

366
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:38,740
With this one?

367
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:40,060
You can drape it over yourself.

368
00:12:40,390 --> 00:12:43,070
(Celebrity)
Like the celebrity

369
00:12:43,070 --> 00:12:44,030
and a man draped in a blanket.

370
00:12:45,630 --> 00:12:46,630
Like this. Come on.

371
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:48,420
(One hand in pocket)

372
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:50,420
Where should we go?

373
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:51,190
Where should we do it?

374
00:12:51,630 --> 00:12:52,750
Where do you guys want?

375
00:12:53,670 --> 00:12:54,990
By this frame.

376
00:12:54,990 --> 00:12:56,030
We could take it by the blue flowers.

377
00:12:56,030 --> 00:12:56,710
Sure, then let's do it here.

378
00:12:56,710 --> 00:12:57,670
Sure.

379
00:12:59,710 --> 00:13:01,070
Isn't that a little too far apart?

380
00:13:01,380 --> 00:13:02,150
(Moves closer)

381
00:13:02,150 --> 00:13:03,870
I'm trying to fit you all in the frame.

382
00:13:05,110 --> 00:13:06,030
I'll take it from up here.

383
00:13:06,030 --> 00:13:06,900
(Runs)

384
00:13:07,030 --> 00:13:07,630
Then should we

385
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:08,590
stand on one side?

386
00:13:08,590 --> 00:13:09,780
Come here.

387
00:13:10,910 --> 00:13:11,430
Wow.

388
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,130
Oh my.

389
00:13:12,150 --> 00:13:12,870
Wait.

390
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:13,510
Wow.

391
00:13:13,510 --> 00:13:14,430
This is amazing, girl.

392
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:17,900
(Finding the angle)

393
00:13:22,030 --> 00:13:22,790
How does it look?

394
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:24,630
Looks good.

395
00:13:25,350 --> 00:13:26,510
You even winked.

396
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:28,810
Wow.

397
00:13:29,190 --> 00:13:30,300
Who knew you had that in you?

398
00:13:30,300 --> 00:13:32,190
Let's take one
that's a little funnier, okay?

399
00:13:32,470 --> 00:13:33,350
Sure.

400
00:13:37,710 --> 00:13:39,710
Sure, wait a second.

401
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:42,300
Three, two, one.

402
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:44,830
My expression.

403
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:51,660
(Behind-the-Scenes 11)

404
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:55,700
(Behind-the-Scenes)

405
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:57,380
(Glances)

406
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:00,220
(Fluent)

407
00:14:02,080 --> 00:14:03,100
Wow.

408
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,860
(Shy)

409
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:07,980
(Grab)

410
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:15,690
(Raises hand at the same time)
You go ahead.

411
00:14:16,990 --> 00:14:17,510
Here. That's right.

412
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:20,900
(Leans closer)

413
00:14:24,910 --> 00:14:26,150
Like this.

414
00:14:26,150 --> 00:14:27,500
I showed you once. Did you get it?

415
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:33,670
That's not right.

416
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:34,340
(Laughs)

417
00:14:35,430 --> 00:14:36,150
Yes.

418
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:39,270
This is how the two of us play it.

419
00:14:39,270 --> 00:14:41,350
Like two mice playing the piano.

420
00:14:42,270 --> 00:14:43,750
I'll do it. I'll just do it myself.

421
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:47,220
(Sways)

422
00:14:48,470 --> 00:14:50,190
(Follows)
Let's get moving.

423
00:15:06,660 --> 00:15:11,620
(Behind-the-Scenes 12)

424
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,740
(Behind-the-Scenes)

425
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:15,500
(Leans closer)

426
00:15:16,030 --> 00:15:16,910
Let me see.

427
00:15:16,910 --> 00:15:17,910
Isn't it kind of chubby?

428
00:15:17,910 --> 00:15:18,550
Let me take a look.

429
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:20,620
Not really.

430
00:15:23,750 --> 00:15:24,540
Definitely.

431
00:15:24,540 --> 00:15:25,790
But yeah,

432
00:15:25,790 --> 00:15:27,110
you've definitely
gotten a lot thinner now.

433
00:15:28,350 --> 00:15:29,710
Here, let me take a picture of you guys.

434
00:15:29,710 --> 00:15:30,380
Okay.

435
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:31,140
Three,

436
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:31,740
two,

437
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:32,260
one.

438
00:15:33,030 --> 00:15:34,110
Thanks, Meng.

439
00:15:34,310 --> 00:15:34,950
Thanks.

440
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:36,270
It looks really good.

441
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:37,740
(Turning his head)

442
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:42,150
I was looking in the wrong place again.

443
00:15:42,470 --> 00:15:43,590
Next time,
look at the top of the Polaroid.

444
00:15:43,590 --> 00:15:44,630
That's where I always look.

445
00:15:44,630 --> 00:15:45,670
The white part.

446
00:15:47,230 --> 00:15:48,550
You're really skinny.

447
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:49,620
Look at you.

448
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:50,140
Of course.

449
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:51,020
"A pointed face".

450
00:15:53,670 --> 00:15:54,630
My forehead.

451
00:15:55,950 --> 00:15:56,660
What's wrong with your forehead?

452
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,030
I really can't stand my forehead.

453
00:15:58,030 --> 00:15:59,420
Don't you like the heart shape?

454
00:15:59,990 --> 00:16:01,190
It's such a perfect one.

455
00:16:01,190 --> 00:16:02,910
Look at his forehead. It's a heart.

456
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:04,230
A heart shape.

457
00:16:05,110 --> 00:16:06,630
You did your hair really well.

458
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:08,020
Yeah.

459
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:09,550
My hair is really full.

460
00:16:11,310 --> 00:16:12,100
Here, touch it.

461
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,310
Touch it.

462
00:16:18,030 --> 00:16:19,030
It is.

463
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:27,100
(Behind-the-Scenes 13)

464
00:16:27,470 --> 00:16:29,310
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Do you prefer talking face-to-face

465
00:16:29,310 --> 00:16:30,790
or sitting off to the side?

466
00:16:32,550 --> 00:16:34,470
Face-to-face feels pretty different.

467
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:37,390
I can really see your expressions

468
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:38,950
and reactions.

469
00:16:46,070 --> 00:16:47,150
I feel like

470
00:16:47,510 --> 00:16:49,590
face-to-face is better when two people

471
00:16:49,590 --> 00:16:50,630
are just getting to know each other.

472
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:52,470
Because when we're talking,

473
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,230
we can pick up on

474
00:16:54,230 --> 00:16:56,430
the other person's
subtle reactions and expressions.

475
00:17:00,630 --> 00:17:02,340
Do you usually like eating alone?

476
00:17:02,550 --> 00:17:04,580
Yeah. I really need to break that habit.

477
00:17:09,350 --> 00:17:11,070
Have you felt any differently
these past few days?

478
00:17:12,150 --> 00:17:13,300
About Signal House?

479
00:17:14,590 --> 00:17:16,350
I feel like I've completely adjusted

480
00:17:16,350 --> 00:17:18,070
to this kind of lifestyle.

481
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:20,470
Do you have any allergies?

482
00:17:24,710 --> 00:17:26,350
I might be lactose intolerant.

483
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:28,300
(Nods)

484
00:17:28,300 --> 00:17:29,790
Do you have any allergies?

485
00:17:29,790 --> 00:17:30,340
(Asks)

486
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:31,830
I don't think so. I'm pretty tough.

487
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:33,110
None at all?

488
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:35,070
I don't think I have any.

489
00:17:36,110 --> 00:17:37,830
You don't have any dietary restrictions?

490
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:39,030
None.

491
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:47,900
(Behind-the-Scenes 14)

492
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:49,300
(Behind-the-Scenes)

493
00:17:49,300 --> 00:17:51,630
When I first started watching tennis,

494
00:17:52,470 --> 00:17:54,030
I watched the Australian Open.

495
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:56,110
And the court was this same blue color.

496
00:17:56,390 --> 00:17:57,310
Badminton courts can be blue too.

497
00:17:57,910 --> 00:17:58,710
Okay.

498
00:17:59,470 --> 00:18:01,310
We can play when we get back
to Signal House.

499
00:18:01,590 --> 00:18:03,390
(Invitation)
The badminton court downstairs? Okay.

500
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:07,270
Badminton looks really fun.

501
00:18:08,070 --> 00:18:09,470
They're fun in different ways.

502
00:18:10,830 --> 00:18:12,100
But in terms of how much
you have to move,

503
00:18:12,100 --> 00:18:12,990
I feel like

504
00:18:13,740 --> 00:18:14,620
it's about the same.

505
00:18:14,620 --> 00:18:15,350
With badminton,

506
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:17,590
you probably know certain positions

507
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:18,710
and know how to move around.

508
00:18:19,270 --> 00:18:20,180
Tell me about it.

509
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:21,390
Like, which positions?

510
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:23,870
(Curious)
In badminton,

511
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:26,070
you practice four-way footwork.

512
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:27,020
And when you play singles,

513
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:28,220
after you return a shot,

514
00:18:28,220 --> 00:18:29,340
you need to get back to the center.

515
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:30,590
From the center,

516
00:18:30,590 --> 00:18:32,110
you can reach anywhere fastest.

517
00:18:33,830 --> 00:18:34,630
As for tennis,

518
00:18:34,630 --> 00:18:35,830
I honestly don't know
how to play at all.

519
00:18:36,670 --> 00:18:38,190
But I've played badminton before.

520
00:18:38,190 --> 00:18:38,950
The coach said that wouldn't work.

521
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:40,230
He said the two

522
00:18:40,230 --> 00:18:41,470
aren't the same thing.

523
00:18:42,670 --> 00:18:43,390
But

524
00:18:43,390 --> 00:18:45,430
they look so similar

525
00:18:45,430 --> 00:18:45,950
that it's hard

526
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:46,870
not to associate the two.

527
00:18:46,870 --> 00:18:48,070
Your body just reacts instinctively

528
00:18:48,070 --> 00:18:49,710
and you end up returning it that way.

529
00:18:50,430 --> 00:18:51,020
So I was thinking,

530
00:18:51,020 --> 00:18:52,460
I guess I really do

531
00:18:53,270 --> 00:18:55,110
need to properly

532
00:18:55,110 --> 00:18:56,630
tell these two sports apart.

533
00:18:57,270 --> 00:18:58,070
It's okay.

534
00:18:58,070 --> 00:18:59,070
As long as we're having fun.

535
00:18:59,190 --> 00:19:00,310
I think I'm having a lot of fun.

536
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:08,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 15)

537
00:19:08,380 --> 00:19:09,580
(Behind-the-Scenes)

538
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:10,350
I'm going out for a bit.

539
00:19:10,630 --> 00:19:11,070
Why?

540
00:19:11,390 --> 00:19:12,270
I'll be right back.

541
00:19:12,430 --> 00:19:12,970
Wait for me.

542
00:19:12,970 --> 00:19:13,890
(Getting ready to go together)
It's okay.

543
00:19:13,910 --> 00:19:14,590
No.

544
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:15,540
Stay here.

545
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:16,220
I have to...

546
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:16,860
No.

547
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:17,630
(Worried about Fang's foot)

548
00:19:17,630 --> 00:19:18,750
I'll be right back.

549
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:19,870
You're going out to get medicine.

550
00:19:19,870 --> 00:19:20,910
(Guessed right)

551
00:19:20,910 --> 00:19:21,550
Stay here.

552
00:19:22,510 --> 00:19:23,110
Okay?

553
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:26,660
(Pinch)

554
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:31,750
(Holding her up)
Watch your foot.

555
00:19:33,230 --> 00:19:34,670
I'll be right back.

556
00:19:34,670 --> 00:19:35,300
Okay.

557
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:38,100
(Heading out to get medicine)

558
00:19:41,780 --> 00:19:42,460
(Arriving at the pharmacy)

559
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,030
Hi.

560
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,270
Do you have anything for pain?

561
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:45,590
It's just

562
00:19:45,590 --> 00:19:47,070
that her toenail is slightly lifted.

563
00:19:47,070 --> 00:19:49,470
Is there something to apply or take?

564
00:19:49,470 --> 00:19:50,870
For something to take, ibuprofen.

565
00:19:50,870 --> 00:19:52,310
(Carefully asking)
Is there anything to apply?

566
00:19:52,310 --> 00:19:53,670
An anti-inflammatory.

567
00:19:53,670 --> 00:19:55,950
But her toenail is lifted.

568
00:19:55,950 --> 00:19:57,310
Can she apply it?

569
00:19:57,310 --> 00:19:58,070
Yes, she can.

570
00:19:58,070 --> 00:19:59,390
Then I'll take both.

571
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:00,160
Okay?

572
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:02,030
I want both.

573
00:20:03,430 --> 00:20:04,350
Okay. Payment done.

574
00:20:04,350 --> 00:20:04,980
Thanks.

575
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:11,940
(Back to Signal House)

576
00:20:15,870 --> 00:20:17,790
You're finally back.

577
00:20:18,070 --> 00:20:18,870
I'm back.

578
00:20:19,310 --> 00:20:21,470
I already finished cleaning the kitchen.

579
00:20:22,110 --> 00:20:23,670
You did chores again?

580
00:20:24,860 --> 00:20:25,900
I had nothing else to do.

581
00:20:28,430 --> 00:20:29,510
Are we staying here?

582
00:20:29,630 --> 00:20:30,420
Sure.

583
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,030
(Hands over)

584
00:20:32,030 --> 00:20:32,950
There's one to apply and one to take.

585
00:20:33,030 --> 00:20:33,630
Okay.

586
00:20:33,830 --> 00:20:34,220
Thanks.

587
00:20:35,070 --> 00:20:36,230
No problem.

588
00:20:38,460 --> 00:20:43,420
(Behind-the-Scenes 16)

589
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:44,500
(Behind-the-Scenes)

590
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:45,510
How about we take a break?

591
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:46,580
Sure.

592
00:20:46,910 --> 00:20:47,580
Let's sit for a bit.

593
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:48,660
Yeah, let's sit.

594
00:20:51,110 --> 00:20:52,230
We climbed a long way.

595
00:20:53,350 --> 00:20:55,220
With how afraid of heights I used to be,

596
00:20:55,220 --> 00:20:57,110
I wouldn't even dare sit like this.

597
00:20:57,270 --> 00:20:58,470
I wouldn't let any part of my body

598
00:20:58,470 --> 00:21:00,270
leave this platform.

599
00:21:00,270 --> 00:21:01,230
Same here.

600
00:21:01,910 --> 00:21:02,870
But you're much better now.

601
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:04,340
Yeah.

602
00:21:07,510 --> 00:21:09,870
Your feet are already off the platform.

603
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:10,510
Yeah.

604
00:21:10,510 --> 00:21:12,670
I'm just getting used to the height.

605
00:21:13,350 --> 00:21:14,750
We're about to jump off it.

606
00:21:16,350 --> 00:21:18,110
Did you ever imagine you could fly

607
00:21:18,270 --> 00:21:20,190
when you were a kid?

608
00:21:20,430 --> 00:21:21,740
(Curious)
I did. I used to imagine it.

609
00:21:21,900 --> 00:21:22,510
You used to.

610
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:23,340
(Laughing)

611
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:24,830
You can really fly in a minute.

612
00:21:26,780 --> 00:21:27,740
That's terrifying.

613
00:21:28,910 --> 00:21:29,950
Chris.

614
00:21:30,470 --> 00:21:31,420
Hi, Maria.

615
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:33,620
Maria.

616
00:21:33,780 --> 00:21:34,310
Maria,

617
00:21:34,310 --> 00:21:35,030
are you ready?

618
00:21:35,470 --> 00:21:36,350
I'm not ready.

619
00:21:36,590 --> 00:21:37,700
Then I'll wait until you are.

620
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,310
Are you ready?

621
00:21:39,870 --> 00:21:41,180
I'm always ready.

622
00:21:43,750 --> 00:21:44,590
Always ready.

623
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:46,020
Yeah.

624
00:21:47,460 --> 00:21:48,960
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

625
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,390
(SVIP updates every Mon & Tue at noon)

626
00:21:50,390 --> 00:21:52,320
